0.0289]},{"n":"Aino","r":[0.1685,0.6281,0.0361,0.0289]},{"n":"Ineffa","r":[0.212,0.6281,0.0361,0.0289]},{"n":"Ifa","r":[0.0815,0.6807,0.0361,0.0289]},{"n":"Fischl","r":[0.125,0.6807,0.0361,0.0289]},{"n":"Xingqiu","r":[0.1685,0.6807,0.0361,0.0289]},{"n":"Beidou","r":[0.212,0.6807,0.0361,0.0289]}]}]}},"thumb":"content/genshin/builds/ifa/261111-224949/en-1.t.webp","why":{"w":[{"name":"Sunny Morning Sleep-In","text":"Huge EM boosts Swirl DMG and team healing."},{"name":"A Thousand Floating Dreams","text":"Massive EM for reaction DMG and healing."},{"name":"Starcaller's Watch","text":"Very high EM makes it a strong stat stick for Swirl and healing; its shield-based team buff is usually inactive. No reliable shield application from Ifa."},{"name":"Wandering Evenstar","text":"EM secondary stat enhances reactions and healing."},{"name":"Sacrificial Fragments","text":"High EM supports healing and Swirl. Its Skill-reset passive is unreliable because casting Ifa’s Skill does not hit. Use for EM, not the reset."},{"name":"Favonius Codex","text":"Energy Recharge and neutral particles help Burst uptime and team rotations; build CRIT Rate to trigger its passive. Needs on-field CRIT hits."},{"name":"Mappa Mare","text":"Craftable EM option that supports Swirl and healing; its reaction-triggered Elemental DMG bonus mainly helps personal damage. F2P craftable choice."},{"name":"Thrilling Tales of Dragon Slayers","text":"Provides a large ATK buff to the next character after swapping, sacrificing personal EM and healing. Swap directly into an ATK-scaling carry. R5 preferred."}],"a":[{"names":["Viridescent Venerer"],"text":"Best overall for an EM Swirl driver: increases Swirl damage and lowers the RES of swirled Pyro, Hydro, Electro or Cryo.","stats":"EM / EM / EM"},{"names":["Scroll of the Hero of Cinder City"],"text":"Team-buff alternative if someone else already wears Viridescent Venerer; trigger an applicable reaction for elemental DMG buffs.","stats":"EM / EM / EM"},{"names":["Gilded Dreams"],"text":"EM-focused alternative that improves Swirl damage and healing when another Anemo teammate already supplies VV resistance shred.","stats":"EM / EM / EM"}],"t":[{"name":"Cacucu Air Control","members":["Ifa","Ororon","Furina","Sayu"],"text":"Ororon adds Nightsoul and Electro; Furina supplies Hydro and buffs. Sayu adds healing and can hold VV for a CRIT Ifa build.","roles":["Driver / Healer","Off-field DPS / Battery","Off-field DPS / Buffer","Healer / Debuffer"]},{"name":"Storm Chasers","members":["Ifa","Ororon","Xingqiu","Fischl"],"text":"Ifa drives Xingqiu and Fischl while Ororon contributes off-field Electro and Nightsoul points, strengthening Electro-Charged reactions.","roles":["On-field Driver","Off-field DPS / Battery","Off-field DPS / Hydro Enabler","Off-field DPS / Battery"]},{"name":"Moonlit Medevac","members":["Ifa","Ororon","Aino","Ineffa"],"text":"Ororon contributes Nightsoul points; Aino and Ineffa enable Lunar-Charged while Ifa drives, heals and Swirls.","roles":["On-field Driver","Off-field DPS / Battery","Off-field DPS / Enabler","Off-field DPS / Shielder"]},{"name":"Budget Air Ambulance","members":["Ifa","Fischl","Xingqiu","Beidou"],"text":"Accessible Taser-style team: Ifa drives off-field attacks and shreds RES. Without another Nightsoul unit, his reaction buff is weaker.","roles":["On-field Driver","Off-field DPS / Battery","Off-field DPS / Hydro Enabler","Off-field DPS"]}],"v":"EM Swirl Driver: 4pc Viridescent, triple EM, Sunny Morning or Sacrificial Fragments; drive Electro-Charged and heal on-hit.\nAnemo CRIT DPS: 4pc Obsidian Codex; ATK% / Anemo / CRIT with Widsith or Cashflow. Best with a separate VV user.\nTeam Buff Support: 4pc Scroll or TTDS when appropriate; swap directly to an ATK carry. Keep enough EM and ER.\nExtra Healing: Use a Healing Bonus circlet or Prototype Amber for greater sustain, especially with Furina.\nF2P Reactions: Mappa Mare + 4pc Viridescent; pair Hydro/Electro off-field units and prioritize Level 90.",